  "interpretation": "The patch refactors `app/db.py` to replace Pydantic model instantiation with plain dictionary construction for database rows, aiming to reduce serialization overhead. Validation passed with zero semantic mismatches, confirming API contract preservation. However, the runner rejected the change due to insufficient improvement. The candidate mean latency (0.507 ms) is marginally lower than the parent (0.512 ms), yielding a relative improvement of only ~0.94%. This gain is negligible compared to the observed noise (coefficient of variation ~1.4-1.6%), suggesting the optimization did not significantly impact the dominant latency factors, likely SQLite I/O or network overhead. The plan's hypothesis regarding Pydantic overhead was not substantiated by measurable performance gains in this context.",
